{#- The brief of a work object made from an entry on the brain's list (dayflow_orchestrator/brain_list_intake.py):
    the architect's "why this is a work object". Expects `entry` {id, kind, what, assistant_part, when_local, why,
    times}, `concern_text` (the concern in full, or empty), `belief` {belief_key, statement, related} or None,
    `sources` [text] (each email or message the concern came from, verbatim); the entry's `day` and `updated_at`
    (when it was decided, UTC ISO) date it. Times local. -#}
FROM THE BRAIN'S LIST (entry {{ entry.id }}): the brain decided this is needed; how is yours.
- the outcome wanted: {{ entry.what }}
- the assistant's part: {{ entry.assistant_part }}
- when: {{ entry.when_local }} (decided {{ entry.updated_at | local_time }})
- why: {{ entry.why }}
{% if belief %}
It comes from the calendar of {{ entry.day }}{% if entry.times %} ({{ entry.times }}){% endif %}, from the owner's belief [belief:{{ belief.belief_key }}]: {{ belief.statement }}
{%- for r in belief.related %}
  read with: {{ r }}
{%- endfor %}
{% endif %}
{%- if concern_text %}
THE CONCERN IT SERVES, as the brain knows it:
{{ concern_text }}
{% endif %}
{%- if sources %}
WHERE THE CONCERN CAME FROM, word for word:
{% for s in sources %}---
{{ s }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
